00:17:56,220 --> 00:18:01,740
this structure is formed
and becomes a stable cloth,

247
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:05,860
the platelets
contract within this

248
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:09,900
environment and
the cloth shrinks.

249
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:15,420
The fibrin mesh becomes
more compact and

250
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:19,300
overall the edges of
the damaged vessels are

251
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:22,240
brought together.
The fluid is squeezed

252
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:26,280
from the cloth and this
makes it more solid.

253
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:30,260
The fluid which is
squeezed is serum,

254
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:34,080
which in fact is plasma
minus fibrinogen and clotting

255
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:37,080
factors, which have been
removed during clothing.

256
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:43,720
Fibrinolysis or
fibrinolytic cascade.

257
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:48,460
Activation of
coagulation cascade also

258
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,300
activates activates
fibrinolitic cascade to

259
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,720
moderate the size of
the clot being formed.

260
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,440
On this diagram,

261
00:18:56,300 --> 00:19:02,120
please note the activated
factor 12, which acts upon

262
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:05,580
plasma calicrine and
transforms it into calicrine.

263
00:19:05,940 --> 00:19:08,400
Calicrine acts in
concert with tissue

264
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:11,620
plasminogen activator
and urokinase,

265
00:19:12,420 --> 00:19:15,840
transforming
plasminogen into active

266
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:19,020
plasmin, which
subsequently acts upon the

267
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:22,940
fibrin meshwork and
transforms it into soluble

268
00:19:22,940 --> 00:19:26,060
fibrinopeptides,
dissolving the cloth.

269
00:19:26,420 --> 00:19:30,360
Synthetic streptokinase
and neurokinase facilitate

270
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:33,060
transformation of
plasminogen into plasmin.

271
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:36,900
However, the action of
plasmin can be inhibited

272
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:41,320
by tranexamic acid and
alpha 2 antiplasmin.

273
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:47,280
In conclusion, plasmin
is generated by enzymatic

274
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:52,740
catabolism of the precursor
plasminogen, either by a factor

275
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:57,580
12-dependent pathway or
plasminogen activators. The

276
00:19:57,580 --> 00:20:02,800
most important plasminogen
activator is TPA. This

277
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:06,300
is manufactured by the
endothelial cells and is most

278
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:09,920
active when bound to fibrin.
It is a very important

279
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:15,260
therapeutic agent because it's
fibrinolytic activity it's

280
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:18,980
mostly confined to the
sites of recent thrombosis.

281
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:25,760
In summary, hemostasis consists

282
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:28,680
of several phases,
vascular phase,

283
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:32,760
primary hemostasis or
platelet phase which

284
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:35,940
results in formation of
the primary platelet plug,

285
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:39,860
secondary hemostasis
or coagulation phase

286
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:43,200
which results in
formation of a stable

287
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:46,440
secondary platelet plug, and

288
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,740
fibrinolytic phase in which

289
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:51,760
there is dissolution
of the platelet plug

290
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:54,180
and re-establishment
of the blood flow.